4. **Preserve the "hybrid safety layer" pattern**: every place data can come from Supabase
   should still degrade gracefully to a clearly-labeled fallback/error state when Supabase
   is unreachable — but that fallback must now be an explicit "offline / degraded" UI
   state, never a silent swap to invented numbers (see §9, "trustworthy failure handling").
5. **No feature in this prompt may regress another.** After every task, run
   `bun run lint` (or `npm run lint`), `bun run build`, and the new test suite (§10) before
   moving to the next task. If a task cannot be completed without breaking another, stop
   and flag it instead of guessing.
6. Commit in small, reviewable chunks, one per numbered task below, with descriptive
   commit messages referencing the task number (e.g. `feat(dashboard): replace mock-data
   with live Supabase session + profile [Task 2]`).

