## 6. Task 5 — Tracker Agent (backend + frontend, closes the loop after submission)

Right now the workforce stops at `application_agent → END`. Nothing watches a
`submitted`/`under_review` application afterward, even though the dashboard header claims
"6 agents coordinated" and `mock-data.ts` already describes a "Tracker Agent — watches the
journey, monitors source portals, tells you the next best action."

1. **Backend** (`backend/agent_graph.py`):
   - Add a new node `tracker_agent_node(state)` that:
     - Runs for applications with `status in ('submitted','under_review')` belonging to
       the citizen.
     - Since there is no real external government portal to poll in this environment,
       implement it as a deterministic **status-transition watcher + next-best-action
       generator**: it re-reads the application's current `status`, computes "days since
       submission", and (a) writes an `agent_event` summarizing current state
       ("Application SAH-2026-xxxxxx has been under review for 6 days."), (b) if
       `days_since_submission > N` (configurable, default 10) and status is still
       `submitted`, escalates by inserting a `notifications` row of type `warning`
       nudging the citizen, and (c) always returns a `next_best_action` payload (reuse the
       existing `NextAction`/`generateNextAction` shape from `services.ts` so frontend and
       backend agree on the contract — move that shape into `backend/state.py` as a
       Pydantic model `TrackerUpdate` mirroring it, since `state.py` already houses the
       other structured Pydantic contracts like `EligibilityResult`).
     - Add this as a **new, separate LangGraph entry point** invoked on a schedule (not
       inline in the citizen's live orchestration run, since tracking happens *after* a
       run completes) — expose it as a new FastAPI route in `backend/app.py`, e.g.
       `POST /tracker/run` guarded by the same `X-Sahayak-Internal-Secret` header check
       already used for `/run` and `/extract-document`, callable by:
       - a new Supabase Edge Function `supabase/functions/tracker-sweep/index.ts`
         (mirrors the auth/secret pattern of `orchestrate-agent-run/index.ts`) that can be
         invoked either manually by an admin action or via a `pg_cron`/Supabase Scheduled
         Function (document both options in `README.md`; scheduled cron is preferred for
         "real" behavior but manual admin trigger is an acceptable v1 fallback — do not
         silently skip this, pick one and implement it fully).
   - Update `write_agent_event` calls project-wide to use `"Tracker Agent"` as the
     `agent_name` for these events so the frontend's existing agent-name string matching
     (`agentLower.includes("tracker")`) lights up correctly — **note**: `use-agent-run.ts`
     and `assistant.tsx` currently only map `citizen/scheme/eligibility/document/application`
